    <briefdescription>
<para>Generate remarks for matrix operations in a function. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>To generate remarks for matrix expressions, the following approach is used:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_use" kindref="compound">Use</ref> the inlined-at debug information to group matrix operations to the DISubprograms they are contained in.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Collect leaves of matrix expressions (done in <ref refid="structanonymous__namespace_02_lower_matrix_intrinsics_8cpp_03_1_1_lower_matrix_intrinsics_1_1_remark_generator_1a53d241b242a10e4f387b39e4497054db" kindref="member">RemarkGenerator::getExpressionLeaves</ref>) for each subprogram - expression</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>For each leaf, create a remark containing a linearizied version of the matrix expression. The expression is linearized by a recursive bottom-up traversal of the matrix operands, starting at a leaf. Note that multiple leaves can share sub-expressions. Shared subexpressions are explicitly marked as shared(). </para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
